  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Velagapudi Sambasiva Rao, vs Food Safety Officer, on 27 December, 2021 Author: Cheekati Manavendranath Roy Bench: Cheekati Manavendranath Roy The Hon'Ble Sri Justice Cheekati Manavendranath Roy Criminal Petition Nos.885 And 1196 of 2021 Common Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioners are A-2 and A-3 in both the aforesaid cases C.C.No.468 of 2017 and C.C.No.467 of 2017 on the file of the learned Special Judicial First Class Magistrate Court for Mobile, Guntur. They are facing prosecution for the offences punishable under Sections 3(1)(zz)(vi)(xi), 26(2)(i) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short FSS Act) and under Section 59(i) of the FSS Act.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners would submit that this is a covered matter in view of the earlier orders passed by this Court in Criminal Petition Nos.1707 and 1708 of 2019 whereby this Court has [LEAKAGE_MASK] the similar charge sheets registered for the similar offences based on identical facts. Therefore, he would submit that the petitioners, who are similarly placed, are entitled for quash of the proceedings initiated against them and thereby prayed to quash the said charge sheets.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners would submit that this is a covered matter in view of the earlier orders passed by this Court in Criminal Petition Nos.1707 and 1708 of 2019 whereby this Court has [LEAKAGE_MASK] the similar charge sheets registered for the similar offences based on identical facts. Therefore, he would submit that the petitioners, who are similarly placed, are entitled for quash of the proceedings initiated against them and thereby prayed to quash the said charge sheets.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
